From badb1f044f1db1e33dd28bb308b28baf208f725a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <MiaAI-Lab@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 16:20:30 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] MiniMax-M3.1-Flash: coalescing, multi-threaded checkpoint
 streamer (task 0015)

A TP2 rank plans 5.77 million byte runs (98% of them 4-16 KiB) for 91 GiB and the
old streamer read each with its own O_DIRECT pread at queue depth 1, plus 22k
one-at-a-time marker reads. The streamer now folds runs under a 1 MiB gap into
windows of up to 16 MiB, reads them on 6 threads into a ring of buffers while the
calling thread copies finished windows in order, packs each cut tensor into few
puts, and verifies the codebook markers in one sorted pass before any copy.
The old strategy stays as runSerial for the tests and the benchmark.

New: stream_test.zig (byte-for-byte against runSerial), loadbench.zig and the
mm3-loadbench build step (stats, model, pattern and raw read benchmarks).

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QguKy82jHfqdgzDsrrC5xs
Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
